1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,990
Turn off every light. Your phone still knows your face.

2
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:08,290
How? It never needed your light. It brings its own.

3
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:12,210
At the top of the screen, there are three tiny parts.

4
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:15,610
A flood light, a dot projector, and a camera.

5
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:17,610
All three work in infrared.

6
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:21,870
Light just past red, which your eyes can't see.

7
00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:26,450
First, the flood light washes your face in infrared.

8
00:00:26,490 --> 00:00:28,290
Like a flash you can't see.

9
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:31,370
The camera takes a picture, in the dark.

10
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:34,050
But a picture can be fooled.

11
00:00:34,090 --> 00:00:37,430
So the projector fires more than 30,000 dots.

12
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:45,390
On a flat wall, the dots land in a grid. On a face, they bend.

13
00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:48,050
Around your nose, your eyes, your cheeks.

14
00:00:49,050 --> 00:00:53,550
The camera measures how far each dot moved, and turns it into depth.

15
00:00:53,750 --> 00:00:55,730
A 3D map of your face.

16
00:00:56,850 --> 00:01:00,050
A printed photo is flat. Its dots don't bend.

17
00:01:00,410 --> 00:01:02,210
No depth, no unlock.

18
00:01:03,450 --> 00:01:07,650
Your map matches the one stored inside the phone. And it opens.

19
00:01:08,850 --> 00:01:12,310
In the dark, your phone was lighting you up the whole time.

20
00:01:12,550 --> 00:01:14,350
You just couldn't see it.

